{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Build for me.</b> That is, for the purpose that I intend and devise in the rationale of the procedure — for the wicked man did not wish to disclose his knowledge and his stratagems to Balak, for faithfulness had been cut off from them. And Balak did according to Balaam's command, as it is written: ״וַיַּעַשׂ בָּלָק כַּאֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר בִּלְעָם״ (Numbers 23:2) — meaning that he [Balaam] told him to perform a procedure for whatever Balaam intended in the matter. He also intended in the word <b>כַּאֲשֶׁר</b> [as/when] — meaning, immediately upon finishing the matter, without delay."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:56.440924544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}